-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Exemption) (No. 3) Order (G.N. No. S 378/2004; O 3, 2007 Revised Edition), made under s 60(b) of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-exemption-no-3-order-2004/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-OR3.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- It exempts from section 43 a person who receives funds from credit facilities granted by banks or other financial institutions licensed by the MAS, for bona fide commercial purposes.

§ `Paragraph 2: Exemption`

-- src:5 | 2. The Minister hereby exempts from section 43 of the Act any person who receives funds from loans, bank guarantees, letters of credit or other credit facilities granted to or in favour of it, by banks or other financial institutions licensed by the Monetary Authority of Singapore, provided that such funds are intended for bona fide commercial purposes.
@ref para 2 (src:5)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person receives funds from loans, bank guarantees, letters of credit or other credit facilities granted to or in favour of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by banks or other financial institutions licensed by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the funds are intended for bona fide commercial purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`O 3 para 2 the person is exempt from section 43 of the Act, on` MEANS
    IF `the Exemption (No. 3) Order as deposited is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (`the person receives funds from loans, bank guarantees, letters of credit or other credit facilities granted to or in favour of it` AND `by banks or other financial institutions licensed by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` AND `the funds are intended for bona fide commercial purposes`)
    ELSE NOTHING
